    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:4b5ff9b4a37f43cc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "80a4144d3d1f7c95544d77d69f0cc784af62e40409b33ee76f13e308562f6509",
      "text": "Day 3 · Transfer to the airport for your flight to Foz do Iguaçu; arrival and transfer to the hotel, then a tour of the Brazilian side of the falls. On the border of Brazil, Argentina and Paraguay, within a national park of unique flora and fauna, 275 waterfalls, each with its own name, crash into the canyon of the Devil’s Throat; their name means “big water” in Guarani. The contrast between the calm, almost lazy river above the falls and the torrents boiling into the gorge below is stunning: you could watch this spectacle for hours. Optional: the Macuco Safari or the Bird Park (see Optional excursions).",
